#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus percuma IBM tentang maklumat dan pengiraan kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Density matrix basics"
msgstr "Asas matriks ketumpatan"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore semidefiniteness */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore semidefiniteness */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin by describing what density matrices are in mathematical terms, and then we'll take a look at some examples.\n"
"After that, we'll discuss a few basic aspects of how density matrices work and how they relate to quantum state vectors in the simplified formulation of quantum information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mulakan dengan menerangkan apa itu matriks ketumpatan dari segi matematik, kemudian kita akan melihat beberapa contoh.\n"
"Selepas itu, kita akan membincangkan beberapa aspek asas tentang cara matriks ketumpatan berfungsi dan hubungannya dengan vektor keadaan kuantum dalam formulasi ringkas maklumat kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Definition {#definition}"
msgstr "Definisi {#definition}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a quantum system named $\\mathsf{X}$, and let $\\Sigma$ be the (finite and nonempty) classical state set of this system.\n"
"Here we're mirroring the naming conventions used in the \"Basics of quantum information\" course, which we'll continue to do when the opportunity arises.\n"
msgstr ""
"Katakan kita mempunyai sistem kuantum bernama $\\mathsf{X}$, dan biarkan $\\Sigma$ menjadi set keadaan klasik (terhingga dan tidak kosong) bagi sistem ini.\n"
"Di sini kita mengikuti konvensyen penamaan yang digunakan dalam kursus \"Asas maklumat kuantum\", yang akan kita teruskan apabila ada peluang.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the general formulation of quantum information, a quantum state of the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a *density matrix* $\\rho$ whose entries are complex numbers and whose indices (for both its rows and columns) have been placed in correspondence with the classical state set $\\Sigma$.\n"
"The lowercase Greek letter $\\rho$ is a conventional first choice for the name of a density matrix, although $\\sigma$ and $\\xi$ are also common choices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam formulasi umum maklumat kuantum, keadaan kuantum sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ diterangkan oleh *matriks ketumpatan* $\\rho$ yang entrinya adalah nombor kompleks dan indeksnya (untuk baris dan lajur) telah diselaraskan dengan set keadaan klasik $\\Sigma$.\n"
"Huruf Yunani kecil $\\rho$ adalah pilihan nama pertama yang konvensional untuk matriks ketumpatan, walaupun $\\sigma$ dan $\\xi$ juga merupakan pilihan yang biasa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here are a few examples of density matrices that describe states of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Berikut ialah beberapa contoh matriks ketumpatan yang menerangkan keadaan Qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{i}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{i}{8} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{i}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{i}{8} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To say that $\\rho$ is a density matrix means that these two conditions, which will be explained momentarily, are both satisfied:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengatakan bahawa $\\rho$ adalah matriks ketumpatan bermakna kedua-dua syarat ini, yang akan diterangkan sebentar lagi, dipenuhi:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unit trace: $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1$.\n"
msgstr "Surih unit: $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Positive semidefiniteness: $\\rho \\geq 0$.\n"
msgstr "Semipositif pasti: $\\rho \\geq 0.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trace of a matrix {#the-trace-of-a-matrix}"
msgstr "Surih matriks {#the-trace-of-a-matrix}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first condition on density matrices refers to the *trace* of a matrix.\n"
"This is a function that is defined, for all square matrices, as the sum of the diagonal entries:\n"
msgstr ""
"Syarat pertama pada matriks ketumpatan merujuk kepada *surih* sebuah matriks.\n"
"Ini adalah fungsi yang ditakrifkan, untuk semua matriks segi empat sama, sebagai jumlah entri pepenjuru:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{0,0} & \\alpha_{0,1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{0,n-1}\\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{1,0} & \\alpha_{1,1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{1,n-1}\\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1,0} & \\alpha_{n-1,1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{n-1,n-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\alpha_{0,0} + \\alpha_{1,1} + \\cdots + \\alpha_{n-1,n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{0,0} & \\alpha_{0,1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{0,n-1}\\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{1,0} & \\alpha_{1,1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{1,n-1}\\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1,0} & \\alpha_{n-1,1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{n-1,n-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\alpha_{0,0} + \\alpha_{1,1} + \\cdots + \\alpha_{n-1,n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trace is a *linear* function: for any two square matrices $A$ and $B$ of the same size, and any two complex numbers $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, the following equation is always true.\n"
msgstr "Surih adalah fungsi yang *linear*: untuk mana-mana dua matriks segi empat sama $A$ dan $B$ bersaiz sama, dan mana-mana dua nombor kompleks $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$, persamaan berikut sentiasa benar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\alpha A + \\beta B) = \\alpha \\operatorname{Tr}(A) + \\beta\\operatorname{Tr}(B)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\alpha A + \\beta B) = \\alpha \\operatorname{Tr}(A) + \\beta\\operatorname{Tr}(B)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trace is an extremely important function and there's a lot more that can be said about it, but we'll wait until the need arises to say more.\n"
msgstr "Surih adalah fungsi yang amat penting dan banyak lagi yang boleh dikatakan tentangnya, tetapi kita akan menunggu sehingga keperluan timbul untuk mengatakan lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Positive semidefinite matrices {#positive-semidefinite-matrices}"
msgstr "Matriks semipositif pasti {#positive-semidefinite-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second condition refers to the property of a matrix being *positive semidefinite*, which is a fundamental concept in quantum information theory and in many other subjects.\n"
"A matrix $P$ is *positive semidefinite* if there exists a matrix $M$ such that\n"
msgstr ""
"Syarat kedua merujuk kepada sifat matriks yang *semipositif pasti*, iaitu konsep asas dalam teori maklumat kuantum dan dalam banyak subjek lain.\n"
"Matriks $P$ adalah *semipositif pasti* jika wujud matriks $M$ sedemikian sehingga\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P = M^{\\dagger} M.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P = M^{\\dagger} M.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we can either demand that $M$ is a square matrix of the same size as $P$ or allow it to be non-square — we obtain the same class of matrices either way.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita boleh sama ada menuntut bahawa $M$ adalah matriks segi empat sama bersaiz sama dengan $P$ atau membenarkannya tidak segi empat sama — kita mendapat kelas matriks yang sama dalam kedua-dua kes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are several alternative (but equivalent) ways to define this condition, including these:\n"
msgstr "Terdapat beberapa cara alternatif (tetapi setara) untuk mentakrifkan syarat ini, termasuk:\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A matrix $P$ is positive semidefinite if and only if $P$ is Hermitian (that is, equal to its own conjugate transpose) and all of its eigenvalues are nonnegative real numbers. Checking that a matrix is Hermitian and all of its eigenvalues are nonnegative is a simple computational way to verify that it's positive semidefinite.\n"
msgstr "Matriks $P$ adalah semipositif pasti jika dan hanya jika $P$ adalah Hermitian (iaitu, sama dengan transpos konjugat sendirinya) dan semua nilai eigennya adalah nombor nyata tidak negatif. Menyemak bahawa matriks adalah Hermitian dan semua nilai eigennya tidak negatif adalah cara pengiraan mudah untuk mengesahkan ia semipositif pasti.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A matrix $P$ is positive semidefinite if and only if $\\langle \\psi \\vert P \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0$ for every complex vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ having the same indices as the rows and columns of $P$.\n"
msgstr "Matriks $P$ adalah semipositif pasti jika dan hanya jika $\\langle \\psi \\vert P \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0$ untuk setiap vektor kompleks $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang mempunyai indeks yang sama dengan baris dan lajur $P$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An intuitive way to think about positive semidefinite matrices is that they're like matrix analogues of nonnegative real numbers.\n"
"That is, positive semidefinite matrices are to complex square matrices as nonnegative real numbers are to complex numbers.\n"
"For example, a complex number $\\alpha$ is a nonnegative real number if and only if\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara intuitif untuk memikirkan tentang matriks semipositif pasti ialah ia seperti analog matriks bagi nombor nyata tidak negatif.\n"
"Iaitu, matriks semipositif pasti adalah bagi matriks segi empat sama kompleks seperti nombor nyata tidak negatif adalah bagi nombor kompleks.\n"
"Contohnya, nombor kompleks $\\alpha$ adalah nombor nyata tidak negatif jika dan hanya jika\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = \\overline{\\beta} \\beta\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = \\overline{\\beta} \\beta\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for some complex number $\\beta$, which matches the definition of positive semidefiniteness when we replace matrices with scalars.\n"
"While matrices are more complicated objects than scalars in general, this is nevertheless a helpful way to think about positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk suatu nombor kompleks $\\beta$, yang sepadan dengan definisi semipositif pasti apabila kita menggantikan matriks dengan skalar.\n"
"Walaupun matriks adalah objek yang lebih kompleks daripada skalar secara amnya, ini tetap merupakan cara yang berguna untuk memikirkan tentang matriks semipositif pasti.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This also explains the common notation $P\\geq 0$, which indicates that $P$ is positive semidefinite.\n"
"Notice in particular that $P\\geq 0$ does *not* mean that each entry of $P$ is nonnegative in this context;\n"
"there are positive semidefinite matrices having negative entries, as well as matrices whose entries are all positive that are not positive semidefinite.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini juga menjelaskan notasi biasa $P\\geq 0$, yang menunjukkan bahawa $P$ adalah semipositif pasti.\n"
"Perhatikan khususnya bahawa $P\\geq 0$ *tidak* bermakna setiap entri $P$ adalah tidak negatif dalam konteks ini;\n"
"terdapat matriks semipositif pasti yang mempunyai entri negatif, serta matriks yang semua entrinya positif tetapi tidak semipositif pasti.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpretation of density matrices {#interpretation-of-density-matrices}"
msgstr "Tafsiran matriks ketumpatan {#interpretation-of-density-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, the definition of density matrices may seem rather arbitrary and abstract, as we have not yet associated any meaning with these matrices or their entries.\n"
"The way density matrices work and can be interpreted will be clarified as the lesson continues, but for now it may be helpful to think about the entries of density matrices in the following (somewhat informal) way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada ketika ini, definisi matriks ketumpatan mungkin kelihatan agak sewenang-wenang dan abstrak, kerana kita belum mengaitkan sebarang makna dengan matriks ini atau entrinya.\n"
"Cara matriks ketumpatan berfungsi dan boleh ditafsirkan akan diperjelaskan apabila pelajaran berlanjutan, tetapi buat masa ini mungkin berguna untuk memikirkan tentang entri matriks ketumpatan dengan cara berikut (yang agak tidak formal).\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The *diagonal* entries of a density matrix give us the probabilities for each classical state to appear if we perform a standard basis measurement — so we can think about these entries as describing the \"weight\" or \"likelihood\" associated with each classical state.\n"
msgstr "Entri *pepenjuru* matriks ketumpatan memberikan kita kebarangkalian bagi setiap keadaan klasik muncul jika kita melakukan pengukuran asas standard — jadi kita boleh memikirkan entri ini sebagai menggambarkan \"berat\" atau \"kemungkinan\" yang dikaitkan dengan setiap keadaan klasik.\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The *off-diagonal* entries of a density matrix describe the degree to which the two classical states corresponding to that entry (meaning the one corresponding to the row and the one corresponding to the column) are in quantum superposition, as well as the relative phase between them.\n"
msgstr "Entri *luar pepenjuru* matriks ketumpatan menggambarkan darjah di mana dua keadaan klasik yang sepadan dengan entri tersebut (iaitu yang sepadan dengan baris dan yang sepadan dengan lajur) berada dalam superposisi kuantum, serta fasa relatif antara keduanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is certainly not obvious *a priori* that quantum states should be represented by density matrices.\n"
"Indeed, there is a sense in which the choice to represent quantum states by density matrices leads naturally to the entire mathematical description of quantum information.\n"
"Everything else about quantum information actually follows pretty logically from this one choice!\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudah tentu tidak jelas *a priori* bahawa keadaan kuantum harus diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan.\n"
"Sesungguhnya, ada satu makna di mana pilihan untuk mewakili keadaan kuantum dengan matriks ketumpatan membawa secara semula jadi kepada keseluruhan penerangan matematik maklumat kuantum.\n"
"Segala-galanya tentang maklumat kuantum sebenarnya mengikuti secara logik daripada satu pilihan ini!\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connection to quantum state vectors {#connection-to-quantum-state-vectors}"
msgstr "Hubungan dengan vektor keadaan kuantum {#connection-to-quantum-state-vectors}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ describing a quantum state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is a column vector having Euclidean norm equal to $1$ whose entries have been placed in correspondence with the classical state set $\\Sigma$.\n"
"The density matrix representation $\\rho$ of the same state is defined as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahawa vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang menerangkan keadaan kuantum $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah vektor lajur yang mempunyai norma Euclidean sama dengan $1$ yang entrinya telah diselaraskan dengan set keadaan klasik $\\Sigma$.\n"
"Perwakilan matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ bagi keadaan yang sama ditakrifkan seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, we're multiplying a column vector to a row vector, so the result is a square matrix whose rows and columns correspond to $\\Sigma$.\n"
"Matrices of this form, in addition to being density matrices, are always projections and have rank equal to $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk jelasnya, kita mendarab vektor lajur dengan vektor baris, jadi hasilnya adalah matriks segi empat sama yang baris dan lajurnya sepadan dengan $\\Sigma$.\n"
"Matriks berbentuk ini, selain daripada menjadi matriks ketumpatan, sentiasa merupakan unjuran dan mempunyai pangkat sama dengan $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, let's define two qubit state vectors.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, mari kita takrifkan dua vektor keadaan Qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[5mm]\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[5mm]\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrices corresponding to these two vectors are as follows.\n"
msgstr "Matriks ketumpatan yang sepadan dengan dua vektor ini adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle{+i}\\vert\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle{-i}\\vert\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle{+i}\\vert\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle{-i}\\vert\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a table listing these states along with a few other basic examples: $\\vert 0\\rangle$, $\\vert 1\\rangle$, $\\vert {+}\\rangle$, and\n"
"$\\vert {-}\\rangle$.\n"
"We'll see these six states again later in the lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah jadual yang menyenaraikan keadaan-keadaan ini bersama beberapa contoh asas lain: $\\vert 0\\rangle,$ $\\vert 1\\rangle,$ $\\vert {+}\\rangle,$ dan\n"
"$\\vert {-}\\rangle.$\n"
"Kita akan melihat keenam-enam keadaan ini lagi kemudian dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| State vector | Density matrix |\n"
"| :---: | :---: |\n"
"| $$\\vert 0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\[1mm] 0 \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert 1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\[1mm] 1 \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {+}\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {+}\\rangle\\langle {+}\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm] \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {-} \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {-}\\rangle\\langle {-}\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm] -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {+i} \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {-i} \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Vektor keadaan | Matriks ketumpatan |\n"
"| :---: | :---: |\n"
"| $$\\vert 0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\[1mm] 0 \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert 1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\[1mm] 1 \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {+}\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {+}\\rangle\\langle {+}\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm] \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {-} \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {-}\\rangle\\langle {-}\\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm] -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {+i} \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm] \\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"
"| $$\\vert {-i} \\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}$$ | $$\\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{i}{2}\\\\[2mm] -\\frac{i}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$$ |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For one more example, here's a state from the *Single systems* lesson of the \"Basics of quantum information\" course, including both its state vector and density matrix representations.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai satu contoh lagi, berikut ialah keadaan dari pelajaran *Sistem tunggal* dalam kursus \"Asas maklumat kuantum\", termasuk kedua-dua perwakilan vektor keadaan dan matriks ketumpatannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert v\\rangle = \\frac{1 + 2 i}{3}\\,\\vert 0\\rangle - \\frac{2}{3}\\,\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\vert v\\rangle\\langle v\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{5}{9} & \\frac{-2 - 4 i}{9}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{-2 + 4 i}{9} & \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert v\\rangle = \\frac{1 + 2 i}{3}\\,\\vert 0\\rangle - \\frac{2}{3}\\,\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\vert v\\rangle\\langle v\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{5}{9} & \\frac{-2 - 4 i}{9}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{-2 + 4 i}{9} & \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Density matrices that take the form $\\rho = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert$ for a quantum state vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are known as *pure states*.\n"
"Not every density matrix can be written in this form; some states are not pure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks ketumpatan yang berbentuk $\\rho = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert$ untuk vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ dikenali sebagai *keadaan tulen*.\n"
"Tidak setiap matriks ketumpatan boleh ditulis dalam bentuk ini; ada keadaan yang bukan tulen.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As density matrices, pure states always have one eigenvalue equal to $1$ and all other eigenvalues equal to $0$.\n"
"This is consistent with the interpretation that the eigenvalues of a density matrix describe the randomness or uncertainty inherent to that state.\n"
"In essence, there's no uncertainty for a pure state $\\rho = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert$ — the state is definitely $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai matriks ketumpatan, keadaan tulen sentiasa mempunyai satu nilai eigen sama dengan $1$ dan semua nilai eigen lain sama dengan $0$.\n"
"Ini konsisten dengan tafsiran bahawa nilai eigen matriks ketumpatan menggambarkan kerawakan atau ketidakpastian yang wujud dalam keadaan tersebut.\n"
"Pada dasarnya, tiada ketidakpastian untuk keadaan tulen $\\rho = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert$ — keadaannya pasti adalah $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, for a quantum state vector\n"
msgstr "Secara amnya, untuk vektor keadaan kuantum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_0\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_0\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for a system with $n$ classical states, the density matrix representation of the same state is as follows.\n"
msgstr "untuk sistem dengan $n$ keadaan klasik, perwakilan matriks ketumpatan bagi keadaan yang sama adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"& =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[10mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\vert\\alpha_0\\vert^2 & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\vert\\alpha_1\\vert^2 & \\cdots & \\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\vert\\alpha_{n-1}\\vert^2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"& =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[10mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\vert\\alpha_0\\vert^2 & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\alpha_0 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\vert\\alpha_1\\vert^2 & \\cdots & \\alpha_1 \\overline{\\alpha_{n-1}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_0} & \\alpha_{n-1} \\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\cdots & \\vert\\alpha_{n-1}\\vert^2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So, for the special case of pure states, we can verify that the diagonal entries of a density matrix describe the probabilities that a standard basis measurement would output each possible classical state.\n"
msgstr "Jadi, untuk kes khas keadaan tulen, kita boleh mengesahkan bahawa entri pepenjuru matriks ketumpatan menggambarkan kebarangkalian bahawa pengukuran asas standard akan menghasilkan setiap keadaan klasik yang mungkin.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A final remark about pure states is that density matrices eliminate the degeneracy concerning *global phases* found for quantum state vectors.\n"
"Suppose we have two quantum state vectors that differ by a global phase:\n"
"$\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle = e^{i \\theta} \\vert \\psi \\rangle$, for some real number $\\theta$.\n"
"Because they differ by a global phase, these vectors represent exactly the same quantum state, despite the fact that the vectors may be different.\n"
"The density matrices that we obtain from these two state vectors, on the other hand, are identical.\n"
msgstr ""
"Catatan akhir tentang keadaan tulen ialah matriks ketumpatan menghapuskan degenerasi berkenaan *fasa global* yang terdapat pada vektor keadaan kuantum.\n"
"Katakan kita mempunyai dua vektor keadaan kuantum yang berbeza dengan fasa global:\n"
"$\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ dan $\\vert \\phi \\rangle = e^{i \\theta} \\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ untuk suatu nombor nyata $\\theta.$\n"
"Kerana ia berbeza dengan fasa global, vektor-vektor ini mewakili keadaan kuantum yang sama persis, walaupun vektor-vektornya mungkin berbeza.\n"
"Matriks ketumpatan yang kita peroleh daripada dua vektor keadaan ini, sebaliknya, adalah sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle \\langle \\phi \\vert =\n"
"\\bigl( e^{i\\theta} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( e^{i\\theta} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= e^{i(\\theta - \\theta)} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle \\langle \\phi \\vert =\n"
"\\bigl( e^{i\\theta} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( e^{i\\theta} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= e^{i(\\theta - \\theta)} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, density matrices provide a unique representation of quantum states:\n"
"two quantum states are identical, generating exactly the same outcome statistics for every possible measurement that can be performed on them, if and only if their density matrix representations are equal.\n"
"Using mathematical parlance, we can express this by saying that density matrices offer a *faithful* representation of quantum states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara amnya, matriks ketumpatan memberikan perwakilan unik bagi keadaan kuantum:\n"
"dua keadaan kuantum adalah sama, menghasilkan statistik hasil yang sama persis untuk setiap pengukuran yang mungkin dilakukan ke atas keduanya, jika dan hanya jika perwakilan matriks ketumpatan mereka adalah sama.\n"
"Menggunakan istilah matematik, kita boleh menyatakan ini dengan mengatakan bahawa matriks ketumpatan menawarkan perwakilan yang *setia* bagi keadaan kuantum.\n"
